{
  "id": "al12",
  "title": "Sense Switches",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al12-l1",
      "title": "IN 377",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "The upper 8 switches on the Altair's panel (A15 to A8) are the sense switches. A program can read them with IN 377 (333, 377): their setting lands in A.",
        "That was the Altair's only input without extra cards: you flipped switches while the program ran.",
        "In this app, the switch settings come from the test, one for each IN 377."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "333   ; 000: IN 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "323   ; 002: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "333   ; 004: IN 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "306   ; 006: ADI",
          "001   ;      1",
          "323   ; 010: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 012: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○●○● = 5",
          "LEDS ○○○○●○●○ = 10"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "00000101",
          "00001001"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does IN 377 do?",
          "options": [
            "Reads the sense switches into A",
            "Shows A",
            "Stops the program",
            "Loads address 377"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "INput from port 377."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e2",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to IN (3 3 3).",
          "answer": 219,
          "explanation": "11 011 011."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Where does the value of IN 377 go?",
          "options": [
            "Into A",
            "Into B",
            "Into memory",
            "Onto the lights"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Like everything else: the accumulator."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "The sense switches are set to 00000110. What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "333   ; 000: IN 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "207   ; 002: ADD A",
            "323   ; 003: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 005: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "12",
            "6",
            "3",
            "0"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "IN reads 6, ADD A doubles it."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How did Altair owners give a program input without extra cards?",
          "options": [
            "By flipping the sense switches",
            "By typing",
            "With a mouse",
            "By talking"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A keyboard needed an interface card and a Teletype."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l1-e6",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Read the sense switches.",
          "code": [
            "___   ; IN",
            "377   ; port 377"
          ],
          "options": [
            "333",
            "323",
            "377",
            "033"
          ],
          "answer": "333",
          "explanation": "IN = 3 3 3, OUT = 3 2 3."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al12-l2",
      "title": "Reacting to the Switches",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Once the switches are in A, all the tools work: ANI to pick out one switch, CPI to compare, and conditional jumps to react.",
        "For example: if switch 0 is up, show all lights, otherwise show none.",
        "Programs read the switches again and again in a loop, so they react while running."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "333   ; 000: IN 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "346   ; 002: ANI",
          "001   ;      1",
          "312   ; 004: JZ off",
          "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "076   ; 007: MVI A",
          "377   ;      255",
          "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 013: HLT",
          "257   ; 014: XRA A   ← off",
          "323   ; 015: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 017: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ●●●●●●●● = 255"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "00000011"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al12-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How do you check whether sense switch 3 is up?",
          "options": [
            "IN 377, ANI 00001000, then look at the zero flag",
            "IN 3",
            "CPI 3",
            "RLC three times"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The mask picks out switch 3."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "After IN 377 and ANI 1, the zero flag is set. What does that mean?",
          "options": [
            "Switch 0 is down",
            "Switch 0 is up",
            "All switches are down",
            "The program stops"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "AND gave 0, so bit 0 was 0."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "The sense switches show 00000011. What do the lights show?",
          "code": [
            "333   ; 000: IN 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "346   ; 002: ANI",
            "001   ;      1",
            "312   ; 004: JZ off",
            "014   ;      address 014 (low byte)",
            "000   ;      (high byte)",
            "076   ; 007: MVI A",
            "377   ;      255",
            "323   ; 011: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 013: HLT",
            "257   ; 014: XRA A   ← off",
            "323   ; 015: OUT 377",
            "377   ;      port 377",
            "166   ; 017: HLT"
          ],
          "options": [
            "255",
            "0",
            "3",
            "1"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Switch 0 is up, so JZ doesn't jump."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l2-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Pick out switch 7.",
          "code": [
            "333   ; IN",
            "377   ; port 377",
