            "001",
            "377"
          ],
          "answer": "200",
          "explanation": "Bit 7 = 10 000 000 = octal 200."
        },
        {
          "id": "al12-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why do real Altair programs read the switches in a loop?",
          "options": [
            "So they can react while running",
            "IN only works in loops",
            "To save memory",
            "They don't"
