          "answer": 4,
          "explanation": "00000100."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "al12-l3",
      "title": "Kill the Bit",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "In 1975, Dean McDaniel wrote a tiny game for the Altair: Kill the Bit. A single light runs across the panel. You flip the sense switch under it at the right moment to shoot it. Miss, and you create another bit.",
        "The trick is XRA: the switches are XORed into the pattern. A switch under a lit bit turns it off, a switch under a dark bit turns one on.",
        "Here, a few rounds of it: rotate the bit, read the switches, XOR, show."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "006   ; 000: MVI B",
          "001   ;      1",
          "016   ; 002: MVI C",
          "003   ;      3",
          "170   ; 004: MOV A,B   ← round",
          "007   ; 005: RLC",
          "107   ; 006: MOV B,A",
          "333   ; 007: IN 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "250   ; 011: XRA B",
          "107   ; 012: MOV B,A",
          "323   ; 013: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "015   ; 015: DCR C",
          "302   ; 016: JNZ round",
          "004   ;      address 004 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "166   ; 021: HLT"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○○○●○ = 2",
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○○ = 0",
          "LEDS ○○○○○○○○ = 0"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "00000000",
          "00000100",
          "00000000"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al12-l3-e1",
